203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Eagle Row lodges and houses are traditionally sorority/fraternity facilities. Exchange students seeking a uniquely American collegiate experience should consider.  Each facility houses 20 to 40 students in a double-occupancy room configuration.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Clairmont Campus:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Apartment-style housing is on campus west of Clairmont Road, connected to the Clifton Road campus via Emory Shuttle.  Each apartment contains a bedroom\(s\), a common living area, a kitchen, and laundry facilities. 2 to 4 students reside in each apartment.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
